; Loose-CBOR `any` positions: every position that lowers CDDL `any` to the AnyCbor static-runtime
; type. Snapshotted under default / preserve / preserve+canonical / json by the `whole_program`
; suite (all `--wasm=false`, since a wasm crate is not a source snapshot). `any` is a full-surface
; citizen — the wasm AnyCbor wrapper landed in loose-CBOR phase A3 WP3, so the `--wasm=true` leg is
; swept by the corpus axis of `wasm_api_parity`, and the JSON flags by the `any_positions_json`
; snapshot leg.
;
; Non-choice positions (A2): member value, array element, table domain/range, top-level alias, tag.
; Type-choice-arm positions (A3): a BARE `any` catch-all in LAST position (forced-backtracking
; dispatch — a typed arm matching on wire type but failing on content falls through to `any`), and a
; TAGGED `any` arm (`#6.n(any)`, cbor_types = [Tag]) which type-dispatches like any tagged arm and so
; is allowed in any position.
member_map = {1: any, ? 2: uint}   ; struct-map member value
member_array = [any, uint]         ; array-record member value
homog_array = [* any]              ; homogeneous array element
table_any_any = {* any => any}     ; table domain AND range
table_uint_any = {* uint => any}   ; table range
table_any_uint = {* any => uint}   ; table domain
top_alias = any                    ; top-level alias
tagged = #6.11(any)                ; tagged
choice_last_any = uint / tstr / any ; type-choice with a bare `any` catch-all arm (last position)
choice_tagged_any = #6.11(any) / tstr ; tagged-`any` type-choice arm (any position; not a catch-all)
